[{"id":126400,"sender_id":612,"sender_full_name":"nLab edit announcer","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/c58b62e30f75d369349d5c08eee8f6b9?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/Morse.20lemma/near/126400\">#1</a> A critical point whose Hessian matrix is nonsingular is usually called a nondegenerate critical point, not a regular critical point - this last term is confusing, since “regular point” is usually reserved for any point which is not critical! See Milnor’s Morse Theory.</p>\n<p>jakelai</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/diff/Morse+lemma/7\">diff</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/Morse+lemma/7\">v7</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Morse+lemma\">current</a></p>","timestamp":1794747999,"subject":"Morse lemma","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]},{"id":126401,"sender_id":612,"sender_full_name":"nLab edit announcer","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/c58b62e30f75d369349d5c08eee8f6b9?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/Morse.20lemma/near/126401\">#2</a> Change regular critical point -&gt; nondegenerate critical point.</p>\n<p>jakelai</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/diff/Morse+lemma/7\">diff</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/Morse+lemma/7\">v7</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Morse+lemma\">current</a></p>","timestamp":1794748043,"subject":"Morse lemma","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]}]